# Harness — context and cognition

The interface shapes reasoning. Treat the context window as finite working memory, not unlimited RAM.

## Search and reads

- Prefer **narrow, specific** queries over broad grep that returns huge result sets. If results are large, **refine the query** before pulling more.
- Read source in **slices** (offsets/limits) when files are long. Do not paste entire large files or thousands of lines into chat.
- **Summarize** findings (tables, bullet lists) instead of dumping raw blobs. Quote only the minimum lines needed for decisions.

## Continuity

- For substantive QA work, **read [qa-handoff.md](qa-handoff.md)** at the start of a session and **update it** before ending with what changed, current focus, and next steps.
- Treat **[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md)** as the short map; follow pointers to deeper docs rather than loading everything at once (**progressive disclosure**).

## Tiered context ([docs/harness-map.json](docs/harness-map.json))

- After T0 (`qa-handoff.md`, `AGENTS.md`), match the user’s task language to T1 `match_any_package` entries in [docs/harness-map.json](docs/harness-map.json). Prefer the **clearest single** package when one fits; if several fit or repro/env/repo questions appear, follow the **`rules`** in that file (Jira-key fetch, optional extra read of [docs/corner-platform-map.json](docs/corner-platform-map.json)). Do not load every doc under `docs/` by default.
- For **environment hostnames**, **which Stash repo**, **Jira project choice**, or **prep vs prod code line** questions, open [docs/corner-platform-map.json](docs/corner-platform-map.json) (T1 `corner_platform_map`) **before** guessing; then use MCP to fill gaps.
- Use **T2** (`user-mcp-atlassian`) for live Jira/Confluence once you know which space/subtree applies (`project.json` vs `qa-project.json` vs `corner-platform-map.json` `mcp_scope_recap`).
- For **Figma** URLs, use the workspace **Figma MCP** when the task needs design context and the server is enabled—see [automation/docs/figma-mcp.md](automation/docs/figma-mcp.md) and the `figma_design` T1 package in [docs/harness-map.json](docs/harness-map.json).
- For **Yogi** requirement links (`/requirements/{space}/{KEY}`, `#req-…`), use [yogi-tool/yogi_resolve.py](automation/tools/yogi-tool/yogi_resolve.py) + [yogi-tool/yogi_snippet.py](automation/tools/yogi-tool/yogi_snippet.py) for **small** `snippet_text`; see [automation/docs/yogi-url-resolve.md](automation/docs/yogi-url-resolve.md) (`yogi_requirement` T1). Avoid loading full Confluence page bodies into the model for every tag.

## Multi-turn (clarifications)

- When the user **corrects** or **narrows** a prior message, start your reply with a **one-line restatement of the original task** (from earlier in the thread), then address the correction. Do not drop the parent question or answer **only** the last sentence.

## Outputs

- Tie work to **verifiable** checks when possible (acceptance criteria, repro steps, expected vs actual).
- Keep **scratch** and ephemeral notes under [automation/temp/](automation/temp/). Durable conclusions belong in proper docs or the handoff file.
